ews/these-soldiers-were-buried-in-an-unmarked-grave-during-the-revolutionary-war-now-historians-finally-know-their-names-180989621/</guid></item><item><title>三名科学家凭借一种用光打开和关闭神经细胞的方法获得诺贝尔医学奖，帮助揭开大脑的奥秘</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/trio-of-scientists-wins-medicine-nobel-for-a-method-to-turn-nerve-cells-on-and-off-with-light-helping-to-unravel-the-brains-mysteries-180989618/</link><description>Karl Deisseroth、Peter Hegemann 和 Georg Nagel 因其对称为光遗传学的神经科学革命性技术的贡献而获得 2026 年奖项，该技术使研究人员能够检查活体动物神经元活动和行为结果之间的精确联系</description><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 19:33:54 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/trio-of-scientists-wins-medicine-nobel-for-a-method-to-turn-nerve-cells-on-and-off-with-light-helping-to-unravel-the-brains-mysteries-180989618/</guid></item><item><title>一场新展览揭示了艳粉色托加长袍和花香如何在罗马帝国传递权力</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-exhibition-reveals-how-hot-pink-togas-and-floral-perfumes-conveyed-power-in-the-roman-empire-180989615/</link><description>哥本哈根时装秀探讨古罗马时尚与影响力之间的关系</description><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 19:00:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-exhibition-reveals-how-hot-pink-togas-and-floral-perfumes-conveyed-power-in-the-roman-empire-180989615/</guid></item><item><title>令人惊叹的长有羽毛和翅膀的恐龙化石进一步暗示飞行在“可怕的蜥蜴”中多次进化</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/remarkable-fossil-of-a-feathered-winged-dinosaur-further-hints-that-flight-evolved-multiple-times-among-the-terrible-lizards-180989612/</link><description>该化石属于一种名为小盗龙的恐龙，这种恐龙与鸟类相似，但不是现代鸟类的祖先。一项新的研究发现，这群古代掠食者进化出了与鸟类相似的解剖适应能力，但发展顺序不同</description><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 15:53:34 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/remarkable-fossil-of-a-feathered-winged-dinosaur-further-hints-that-flight-evolved-multiple-times-among-the-terrible-lizards-180989612/</guid></item><item><title>观看 2026 年狗狗摄影奖中令人印象深刻的获奖作品，这些作品中的可爱、忧郁和威严的犬类</titl